From: Enceka <enceka@yeah.net>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: skip host reorder for connac2 RX queues

Connac2 already reorders packets before forwarding them to either the PPE
or its host RX queues. CT keeps this NPU in its own path instead of
mmio.npu, so the existing device-active check misses the CT queues.

Bypass the software BA window for both connac2 queues. Hardware-forwarded
packets never advance that window; applying it again to host exceptions
drops control traffic after sequence wrap and stalls TCP completion.

--- a/mac80211.c
+++ b/mac80211.c
@@ -1595,7 +1595,8 @@
 	while ((skb = __skb_dequeue(&dev->rx_skb[q])) != NULL) {
 		mt76_check_sta(dev, skb);
 		if (mtk_wed_device_active(&dev->mmio.wed) ||
-		    mt76_npu_device_active(dev))
+		    mt76_npu_device_active(dev) ||
+		    q == MT_RXQ_NPU0 || q == MT_RXQ_NPU1)
 			__skb_queue_tail(&frames, skb);
 		else
 			mt76_rx_aggr_reorder(skb, &frames);
